      "desc:8": "The integrated processing trial — the old one-click ore processing dream, rebuilt as a megastructure. One Steam Mineral Logistics Cluster, all seven processing units configured — crusher, washer, centrifuge, thermal centrifuge, sifter, magnetic separator, furnace — and all five amplifier units installed and running.\n\nWire the halls to your hub network with the full compartment set: singularity steam and fluid compartments on the input and output sides, mode-locked, talking only to their hubs. Ore enters one door, finished stacks leave the other, whole chains atomic.\n\nHand in the controller, five amplifiers and the compartment quartet. The chain bill is 8,000 x 1.5^(n-1) L/s per chain — budget your steam accordingly.",
